WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.527
This query counts the rows produced by the GROUP BY approach and the window approach.

00:00:04.527 --> 00:00:09.462
The grouped result has one row per patient.

00:00:09.462 --> 00:00:12.487
The window result has one row per admission.

00:00:12.487 --> 00:00:18.592
Neither is automatically better. They answer different analytical output-grain questions.

00:00:18.592 --> 00:00:24.267
Connect this idea to an operations team comparing each event with the previous and next event.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:29.202
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:29.202 --> 00:00:36.177
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:36.177 --> 00:00:41.197
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:41.197 --> 00:00:46.320
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
